<!--
  Injected into <manifest> via buildozer's android.extra_manifest_xml.

  This replaces the old `android.features = android.hardware.usb.host`
  setting: buildozer turns that key into a p4a command-line switch that
  current python-for-android no longer accepts, and the build dies with
  "unrecognized arguments". Both buildozer 1.5.0 and 1.6.0 emit it, so the
  setting itself has to go; injecting the XML is what p4a supports today.

  required="false" is deliberate - it declares the feature without letting
  Play or other stores filter out devices whose OTG support is not
  advertised, so the APK stays installable everywhere and the app still
  calls the USB host APIs at runtime.
-->
<uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.usb.host" android:required="false" />
